{"actor":{"id":"LCA","name":"Saint Lucia","type":"state","iso2":"lc","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Lucia","coords":[-60.99,14.01],"seat":"Castries","regions":["world"],"card":"full","tier":"minor","dataset":"wikidata","last_verified":"2026-10-16","grand_strategy":{"objectives":[{"rank":1,"text":"Hold the Taiwan tie restored in 2007. Our reading, not a stated aim: the embassy in Taipei opened on 4 June 2015, described as its first in Asia, which is the one visible investment in the tie.","confidence":"C","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foreign_relations_of_Saint_Lucia","title":"Foreign relations of Saint Lucia (read via the Wikipedia API)","publisher":"Wikipedia (index)","date":"2026-10-16","tier":4},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Foreign_relations_of_Taiwan&oldid=1378208098","title":"Foreign relations of Taiwan","publisher":"Wikipedia (index)","date":"2026-10-12","tier":4}]},{"rank":2,"text":"Keep the British and Commonwealth link as the older anchor of its foreign ties. Our reading: diplomatic relations with the United Kingdom since 22 February 1979, high commissions in London and Castries, the CARIFORUM-UK Economic Partnership Agreement, and Commonwealth membership.","confidence":"C","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foreign_relations_of_Saint_Lucia","title":"Foreign relations of Saint Lucia (read via the Wikipedia API)","publisher":"Wikipedia (index)","date":"2026-10-16","tier":4},{"url":"https://thecommonwealth.org/our-member-countries","title":"Commonwealth of Nations - member states","publisher":"Commonwealth of Nations","date":"2026-10-12","tier":1}]}],"means":[{"text":"A small but wide diplomatic network: embassies in Washington and Taipei (opened 2015), a high commission in London, and seats in the Commonwealth, the OAS and the UN. As a CARICOM member it backed US efforts on UN Security Council Resolution 940 regarding Haiti.","confidence":"C","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foreign_relations_of_Saint_Lucia","title":"Foreign relations of Saint Lucia (read via the Wikipedia API)","publisher":"Wikipedia (index)","date":"2026-10-16","tier":4}]}],"constraints":[{"text":"Drug transit. Its use as a transit point for South American drugs bound for the United States and Europe is the source of the tension in its US relation, per the Wikipedia lead.","confidence":"C","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foreign_relations_of_Saint_Lucia","title":"Foreign relations of Saint Lucia (read via the Wikipedia API)","publisher":"Wikipedia (index)","date":"2026-10-16","tier":4}]}],"paradoxes":[{"text":"The Taiwan recognition has changed hands twice since 1984 (Taipei to Beijing in 1997, back to Taipei in 2007), and the 2015 embassy in Taipei binds it to a recognition that its own history shows can be reversed. Our reading.","confidence":"C","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foreign_relations_of_Saint_Lucia","title":"Foreign relations of Saint Lucia (read via the Wikipedia API)","publisher":"Wikipedia (index)","date":"2026-10-16","tier":4},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Foreign_relations_of_Taiwan&oldid=1378208098","title":"Foreign relations of Taiwan","publisher":"Wikipedia (index)","date":"2026-10-12","tier":4}]}],"reading":"Saint Lucia runs a small but wide diplomacy: embassies in Washington and Taipei, a high commission in London, and seats in the Commonwealth, the OAS and the UN.\nIts Taiwan tie is the choice that matters most (restored in 2007, the Taipei embassy in 2015), and its British and Commonwealth link is the older anchor.\nEvery row here is C because the only source read was Wikipedia (tier 4); the posture grades, the 2025 election, the US citizenship-by-investment pressure and the economy are left open until a sourced pass.\n"},"stale":false},"stances":[],"stances_toward":[],"relations_from":[{"from":"LCA","to":"XKX","layer":"alignment","type":"recognition","summary":"Recognises Kosovo sin